From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:36:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 078/138] pmdomain: apple: Keep the power domains on across
 system suspend

genpd powers off every domain whose devices are all suspended in the
noirq phase of system suspend. On T7000 that is nearly everything that
is not apple,always-on: gpio, ans, pcie_ref, disp0/mipi_dsi, usb*, the
UARTs, I2C and SPI blocks. Linux cannot bring most of them back: the
display pipe and the flash IOP were set up by iBoot, the PCIe link would
need a re-train that pcie-apple does not do on resume, and a GPIO block
that lost power forgets every pin setting and cannot deliver the button
interrupt that is supposed to end suspend-to-idle. The first
"echo freeze > /sys/power/state" would end in a phone that never wakes.

Give the domains a governor whose ->system_power_down_ok() says no, so
genpd_sync_power_off() leaves them alone. Runtime PM and the late_initcall
power-off of unused domains do not consult that callback and behave as
before. pmgr_pwrstate.suspend_power_off=1 (or the sysfs parameter)
restores the old behaviour for experiments with drivers that do restore
their block.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
index 82c33cf72..2986e8383 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
@@ -47,6 +47,29 @@ struct apple_pmgr_ps {
 };
 
 #define genpd_to_apple_pmgr_ps(_genpd) container_of(_genpd, struct apple_pmgr_ps, genpd)
+
+/*
+ * System suspend (s2idle) leaves every domain powered by default. genpd would
+ * otherwise cut each domain whose devices are all suspended, and on A7/A8 most
+ * of the blocks behind them cannot be brought back by Linux: the display pipe
+ * and the flash IOP were set up by iBoot, the PCIe link would need a full
+ * re-train, and losing the GPIO block loses every pin setting and the button
+ * wake path. Runtime PM and the boot-time power-off of unused domains are not
+ * affected.
+ */
+static bool suspend_power_off;
+module_param(suspend_power_off, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(suspend_power_off,
+		 "Let genpd power domains off during system suspend (default: keep them on)");
+
+static bool apple_pmgr_ps_system_power_down_ok(struct dev_pm_domain *pd)
+{
+	return READ_ONCE(suspend_power_off);
+}
+
+static struct dev_power_governor apple_pmgr_ps_gov = {
+	.system_power_down_ok = apple_pmgr_ps_system_power_down_ok,
+};
 #define rcdev_to_apple_pmgr_ps(_rcdev) container_of(_rcdev, struct apple_pmgr_ps, rcdev)
 
 static int apple_pmgr_ps_set(struct generic_pm_domain *genpd, u32 pstate, bool auto_enable)
@@ -249,7 +272,7 @@ static int apple_pmgr_ps_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		regmap_update_bits(regmap, ps->offset, APPLE_PMGR_FLAGS | APPLE_PMGR_AUTO_ENABLE,
 				   APPLE_PMGR_AUTO_ENABLE);
 
-	ret = pm_genpd_init(&ps->genpd, NULL, !active);
+	ret = pm_genpd_init(&ps->genpd, &apple_pmgr_ps_gov, !active);
 	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "pm_genpd_init failed\n");
 		return ret;
